# Specific Engineering Instructions
1. Audit the supplied code across 5 critical dimensions:
   - Correctness & Edge-Case Handling (logic errors, off-by-one, null safety)
   - Security & Input Sanitization (injection, credential exposure, improper auth)
   - Performance & Algorithmic Complexity ($O(n)$ bottlenecks, resource leaks)
   - Maintainability & Idiomatic Style (type hints, naming, decoupling, SOLID)
   - Testability (observability, mockability)
2. Categorize all review findings by severity: [CRITICAL], [WARNING], [SUGGESTION], or [NIT].
3. For each finding, provide the exact problematic lines, concrete technical rationale, and a drop-in replacement snippet.

# Constraints & Rules
- Do NOT provide vague feedback like "looks good" or generic comments; every point must be actionable.
- Focus strictly on verified flaws and measurable quality improvements.
- Respect the existing project coding style and framework versions.

# Expected Output Format
Deliver your response using clean GitHub Flavored Markdown:
1. Executive Review Verdict (Approved / Changes Requested) & Overall Quality Assessment
2. Categorized Review Findings (Severity, Issue, Impact, Recommended Replacement Code)
3. Security & Performance Deep Dive
4. Positive Observations & Commendations
